==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|be-|rate<t:to scold, upbraid>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈɹeɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-berate.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪt|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[chide]] or [[scold]] [[vehemently]].
#: {{ux|en|What society tells people that they can “do whatever they want” to dissidents, and yet '''berates''' anyone for treating them well?}}
#* {{RQ:Parker Seats of the Mighty|chapter=13
|passage=Gabord, still muttering, turned to us again, and began to '''berate''' the soldiers for their laziness.}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Gods of Mars|chapter=21|pages=327–328|pageref=327|passage=A thousand times I '''berated''' myself for being drawn into such a trap as I might have known these pits easily could be.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1917|author=w:Jack London|title=Jerry of the Islands|chapter=14
|passage=Lenerengo, as usual, forgot everything else in the fiercer pleasure of '''berating''' her spouse.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|date=27 Nov 2008|author=Alex Perry|title=The Man Who Would Be (Congo's) King|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110207082649/http://www.time.com/time/world/article/0,8599,1862646,00.html
|passage=During the rally, he '''berates''' the crowd for their cowardice.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2011|author=Tom Fordyce|title=Rugby World Cup 2011: England 12-19 France|site=news.bbc.co.uk|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/rugby_union/15210221.stm
|passage=France were supposedly a team in pieces, beaten by Tonga just a week ago and with coach Marc Lievremont publicly '''berating''' his players, but so clear-cut was their victory that much of the atmosphere had been sucked from the contest long before the end.}}

